RFP Hub Standard v1.0.0 — FROZEN 2026-08-10.

This version's NORMATIVE bytes are immutable: opportunity.schema.json, context.jsonld, the
examples this cut shipped, and the whole conformance suite (../../conformance/v1.0.0/). So are
the versionless artifacts they rest on — ../../meta/, ../../registries/entry.schema.json — and
the identity fields of ../../spec.config.json.

The presence of this file is what .github/workflows/spec-freeze.yml reads (the rule itself is
scripts/spec-freeze.mjs, at the repository root): from here on any PR that edits one of those
artifacts fails.

The INFORMATIVE documents of this directory — FIELDS.md, CROSSWALK.md, BENCHMARK.md, STATUS.md —
stay corrigible, and the gate permits modifying them by name. That is not a loophole, it is the
line ../../NORMATIVE.md draws: those documents carry no conformance weight, and ../../PROCESS.md
says they may be corrected at any time. Freezing them would freeze a broken link and a wrong
crosswalk row into a published version forever. Nothing may be ADDED to or DELETED from this
directory either way.

A breaking change takes a NEW version directory. This one stays published and unedited, forever.
Removing this marker is not a way to land a change — the gate reads it from the base ref, and the
rule it mechanises is in ../../PROCESS.md ("In-place re-cuts") and
adr/0001-recut-v1.0.0-in-place.md.

Declared stable in the same change that adopted the canonical identity on ethrfps.app;
see adr/0007-canonical-domain-and-spec-identity.md and ./STATUS.md.
